> > to compile. I checked that all patches are applied successfully, and they
> > are. Is there something /stupid|silly|crazy/ I may be doing wrong ? 
> 
> I took a look at alloc.c from Apache 1.2:
> 
> static void fd_cleanup (void *fdv) { close ((int)fdv); }
> 
> So it definitly is casting a pointer to an int, but it looks like this
> is being done quite deliberatly.  I suspect that the source of your
> problems is elsewhere.  Also, www.digital.com is running apache, so I
> suspect that all the 64/32 bit problems have been cleaned up.  If I had
> to guess, I would say there is probably a problem in glibc.  Can you run
> the server in the debugger (in the non-forking mode), and see if you can
> get a line number where the crash is occuring?

According to one of the Apache Developers, the int size warnings can be
safely ignored.  I'm running 1..2 without problems, even though I received 
the same warnings.  Supposedly there are patches to allow it to compile
cleanly, just none "...clean enough to be included with the distribution".

Digital runs their webservers on Digital UNIX, not Linux.  Apache
compiles cleanly under DU.

