Subject: Problems building 2.1.42 kernel

we're trying to build linux-2.1.42 on a PC164 (currently running 2.0.30, RH 4.1)
i'm sure i've got the symlinks in /usr/include set correctly and the symlink
'linux' in /usr/src points to the 2.1.42 build tree.  

after make dep, and make boot things barf out on the first obj with:

gcc -D__KERNEL__ -I/usr/src/linux-2.1.42/include -Wall -Wstrict-prototypes -O2 -fomit-frame-pointer -D__SMP__ -pipe -mno-fp-regs -ffixed-8  -c -o init/main.o init/main.c
In file included from init/main.c:17:
/usr/src/linux-2.1.42/include/linux/sched.h:106: parse error before `tasklist_lock'
/usr/src/linux-2.1.42/include/linux/sched.h:106: warning: data definition has no type or storage class
In file included from init/main.c:17:
