Message-ID: <199706170023.UAA04469@churchy.gnu.ai.mit.edu>
Date: Tue, 17 Jun 1997 00:16:23 +0200 (MET DST)
From: Ville Steudle <ville@finland.hb.north.de>
Subject: Re: AIC7XXX speed negotiation
In-Reply-To: <199706161832.OAA07074@crim12b.nsls.bnl.gov>

> i've set the adaptec
> firmare to negotiate up to 40 MHz/sec...
[...]
> of this speed according to their documentation.  when the aic7xxx
> driver negotiates speed, during boot, we only get an indication of
> 20 MHz...

The solution is: You have to do some maths.    :-)

20 MHz data transfer speed * 2 Bytes per transfer (wide = 16 bit)
results in 40 MB/s data transfer rate

As you see, everything is all right - nothing you should change.

Regards, Ville

