>>> "Bruce Embrey" said:
> I have seen this before. You need to build your milo to remove TGA support
> and substitute it with the VGA standard you want.

Actually, it's the *kernel* that needs rebuilding.

MILO *always* has both built in, and *will* choose VGA over TGA, as the
use has indicated (seeing all the messages up to the point where the kernel
starts, on the monitor attached to the VGA).

It's the kernel that chooses TGA over VGA, and thus, the easiest solution
is to build a kernel with *no* TGA support.

