Subject: Re: gimp 0.99.10 on an AXP [sic]

> Hase anyone of you get gimp up and running in an actual version ?? 
> I hab about 2 hors just to get it compiled ... And now it only means

> ** ERROR **: BadAccess (attempt to access private resource denied)
> gimp fatal error: sigabrt caught
> [n]othing, [e]xit, [s]tack trace, [a]ttach to process:
> when I'll load an image :-((
> Anyone done better than me ??

Two things: if you're running on an 8-bit display, turn on
(install-colormap) in ~/gimp/gimprc.  Then, if you're using an older
X-server (such as the 3.1.2 TGA server), then be sure to use option
--no-xshm when invoking gimp.

That should give you a working GIMP.

	--david

